    {
      "text": "From octonions to composition superalgebras via tensor categories — The nontrivial unital composition superalgebras, of dimension 3 and 6, which exist only in characteristic 3, are obtained from the\n\n**From octonions to composition superalgebras via tensor categories**\n\n*Published by EMS Press and licensed under a CC BY 4.0 license*\n\n24 pp, 7 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** The nontrivial unital composition superalgebras, of dimension 3 and 6, which exist only in characteristic 3, are obtained from the split Cayley algebra and its order 3 automorphisms, by means of the process of semisimplification of the sym- metric tensor category of representations of the cyclic group of order 3. Connections with the extended Freudenthal magic square in characteristic 3, that contains some exceptional Lie superalgebras specific of this characteristic are discussed too. In the process, precise recipes to go from (nonassociative) algebras in this tensor category to the corresponding superalgebras are given.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 From algebras to superalgebras; 3 From octonions to composition superalgebras; 4 Semisimplification: skew transformations, de; 5 The extended Freudenthal magic square; References",
